# DeepSeek Chat Exporter (Android)

Hi. This is the Android version of my exporter. Since mobile browsers don't support extensions, I created a bookmarklet. It's a special browser bookmark containing code that works right on the page without installing any apps.

## Features
- Exports the entire chat via API instantly.
- Saves only your prompts and the AI s final answers.
- Formats the text into Markdown.
- Displays the exported text right on your screen so you can copy it to your notes.

## Other Platforms
- For Windows (Edge and Chrome): [deepseek-exporter](https://github.com/SEQUOlA/deepseek-exporter)
- For Mac (Firefox): [deepseek-exporter-mac](https://github.com/SEQUOlA/deepseek-exporter-mac)

## Installation and Usage
You will need Firefox for Android.

1. Open the bookmarklet.js file in this repository and copy the entire code.
2. Open Firefox on your phone and go to any page (e.g., ya.ru).
3. Tap the address bar and start typing any address to trigger the bookmark button, or open the menu (three dots) and select "Add to bookmarks".
4. In the "Name" field, type DS Export.
5. In the "URL" field, paste the copied code. Make sure it starts with javascript: (if the browser removes it, type it manually).
6. Save the bookmark.
7. Go to chat.deepseek.com, log in, and open the chat you want to export.
8. Tap the address bar, type DS, and select your bookmark from the suggestions.
9. A window with the entire chat text will appear. Long-press the text, select "Select all" and "Copy".

